# Everything under repro_package_zp/ is TRACKED VERBATIM.
# Its files are the verification anchors for manifests/CHECKSUMS.txt (sha256),
# so no pattern here may match a path inside it -- with one exception: compiled
# Python caches, which are artefacts of *running* the package and are not part
# of the seal.
#
# ORDER MATTERS.  git applies these in sequence and the last match wins, so the
# blanket negation near the bottom re-includes anything ignored above it.  The
# cache rules are therefore repeated AFTER the negation.

# ---- Python caches ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- Virtual environments ----
.venv/
venv/

# ---- Re-run output (never commit; the archived anchors are already tracked) ----
runs/
tenseed_run/
wd1111_run/
wd1111_battery_run/

# ---- OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ---- LaTeX build products at repo root ----
/*.aux
/*.bbl
/*.blg
/*.fdb_latexmk
/*.fls
/*.out
/*.synctex.gz

# ---- Safety net: the sealed package is never ignored ----
!repro_package_zp/
!repro_package_zp/**

# ---- ...but compiled caches inside it are.  MUST stay after the negation. ----
repro_package_zp/**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
